{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Et.</b> After saying את he added אתו, and its plural is like it, or its sense is אתו לבדו תקדישו, for it is human nature to fear the holy one, as in כי איש אלהים קדוש הוא (2 Kings 4:9):" "<b>Ma'aritzekhem.</b> A noun of attribution, or a verb, i.e., the one who truly terrifies you:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:51.212531336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}